Problem Statement: 
An organization chart has been lost, and only its in order and preorder traversal sequences are available.
Write a C++ program to reconstruct the original binary tree representing the organization chart using the given traversal sequences. 
Display the reconstructed tree in a clear format and verify its correctness by performing in order and preorder traversals on the constructed tree and comparing them with the given sequences.
Objectives: 
-  To write a C++ program to reconstruct a binary tree representing an organization chart using the given in order and preorder traversal sequences.
-  To display the reconstructed tree in a clear and understandable format.
- To verify the correctness of the tree by comparing its in order and preorder traversals with the given sequences.
-  To understand the concepts of binary trees and different tree traversal techniques.
- To use recursion to construct the original tree from the given traversal sequences.
- To understand the practical application of data structures in representing organizational hierarchies.
